  "title": "Finite K1 checks in Lean: P12 one-site kernel cells, rec2 charges, complement-twist tables, stationary 2-column graph",
  "scope": "LEAN-VERIFIED finite statements about the K1 results of Agents 2, 3, 5 and 14, each stated exactly as in reports/audit_2026-10-28/FORMALIZATION_K1.md. (1) K1Kernel*: step_value (the pair-word step computes N + rev N) and, for every a<=18, the pair-word step is unchanged iff a is the published +-9 value, for all 12 phases at n=146/147 (sites 52..60) and phases 0/4/8 at n=400/401 (sites 178..186); local_equations_give_table (table = solution set of the two local carry equations). Not proved: the all-length/all-site theorem or realisability of changed words. (2) K1Charges: rec2 row charges are 0 mod 99 for all 8 rows, consistent with the cyclic bulk update; 22^96 = 55 mod 99; exhaustive charge classification only for (b,M,m) = (10,33,2), (10,9,3), (10,11,3). (3) K1Twist: the mismatch tables per start phase match the published values and the no-complement-return statement holds for all d>=1 by a periodic-reduction lemma; odd-G complement coincidences for rec0/rec1 are recorded (d<=L). (4) K1Stationary: the 2-column transition graph for j mod 5 in {0,3} has no path of 15 (resp. 21) transitions but has one of 14 (resp. 20); the graph is a transcription whose soundness against the real step is NOT formalised. Nothing here claims a Lychrel number or excludes a moving defect front.",
